                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]A short, cute, and extremely hectic FPS.[/b]\n\nThe previews and screenshots don't show what the game is truly about.\nIt's a game where some serious precision and target prioritizing is required, all without an in-game crosshair or an auto-aim. However, each level can be completed in under 30 or 60 seconds, with level restarts being extremely fast, too. The game gets even more hectic if you're going for no-miss and speedrun ranks, which have really strict requirements if you can't find shortcuts and such, especially in the later levels.\nYou can also skip levels you're having trouble with, though that's probably not advised since the game usually gets harder the further in you go. I haven't tested, but I think you can skip all the way to the credits.\n\nThe only real problems I have with the game are the last sets of stages where, if you're not checking online, you spend a lot of time figuring out how to even progress before you can even start improving, whereas in prior levels, you can figure out what you're supposed to do real fast so you can start getting better a lot sooner.\n\nIt's a fun little difficult FPS that might take a few hours to beat, and way longer if you're going for the full completion stuff.",
